# What must never be committed, and why each line is here.
#
# This repository has already paid for the absence of one of these lines: a
# `git add -A` after an install committed 6 366 files and the summary said
# "1 file changed", because nobody looked.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials and machine-local configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env` carries the password hash and the host paths to ~/.kube and ~/.aws. It
# is the one file in the tree whose whole purpose is to differ per machine.
#
# `.env.example` is the opposite — it is the documentation — so it is excluded
# from the exclusion explicitly, because `.env.*` would otherwise swallow it and
# the omission would look deliberate rather than accidental.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# In case one is ever copied in to reproduce something.
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.pem
!**/testdata/**/*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `dist/` and built binaries are never committed.
node_modules/
dist/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/kubetower

# Go test artifacts. `*.test` is a compiled binary, not a source file, and it
# lands beside the package it was built from.
*.test
coverage.out
coverage.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not tidiness. A committed `.idea/` hands every contributor one person's
# absolute paths, and a `.DS_Store` in a public repository is a directory
# listing of somebody's machine.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# A `go.work` points at absolute paths on one machine and silently changes what
# `go build` resolves for anyone who checks it out.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Playwright writes failures here: screenshots, traces, an error context.
# Local by nature - they are about one run on one machine.
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/

# Private working notes, never part of the repository.
*.local
/docs/local/
/.scratch/
